// Canonical ignore set for the pi-agent syncthing folder.
// Both sides symlink this file to ~/.pi/agent/.stignore:
//   - Mac: symlink straight to this repo file. Its mtime is real, so
//     syncthing reloads edits on its own.
//   - box: symlink to the nix store copy, where all mtimes are epoch 0.
//     Syncthing detects .stignore changes by mtime, so it never notices
//     an update. After changing this file, restart syncthing on the box:
//     sudo systemctl restart syncthing
//
// Syncs: the working tree, memory/, settings.json, auth.json, trust.json,
// sessions/ (the box's curation writer reads Mac-side sessions), extensions/
// (hand-written .ts), packages/ (installed plugins, minus their
// node_modules).
//
// (?d) rationale: machine-local dirs must never block a remote delete.
// A remote-deleted directory that still contains ignored files retries
// forever until someone rm's the leftovers by hand (2026-10:
// pi-mcp-adapter under git/ wedged the Mac side exactly so).

// Conflict forks are noise; never index them, never block cleanup.
(?d)*.sync-conflict-*

// Derived session index: a live sqlite DB (shared sqlite + concurrent
// writers = corruption). Each machine rebuilds its own via qmd embed.
(?d)sessions-index

// Machine-local build artifacts. .direnv holds symlinks into the Mac's
// /nix/store; meaningless on the box. node_modules is one pnpm install away.
(?d)node_modules
(?d).pnpm-store
(?d).direnv

// pi's plugin clone dir (git/github.com/<org>/<repo>): where pi clones
// installed plugins. Machine-local install state, same class as
// node_modules — each machine's pi installs its own.
/git

// qmd cache: models + embeddings. Local per machine.
(?d).cache

// Runtime subagent state (pids, sockets) — dead on arrival cross-machine.
(?d).pi-subagents
